  Quote of the Week:

  Saint Ignatius Loyola, Spanish soldier and founder of the Jesuit Order, 
1522:
  "To arrive at the truth in all things, we ought always to be ready to 
believe that what seems to us white, is black if the hierarchical Church so 
defines it."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  Frigid winter melted into fragrant spring.  Dances prepared his armies to 
defend Alberta and the surrounding provinces.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Dances with Goblins for this year.


  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Drago (#39) hiked into Oregon.  He had grown tired with British Columbia 
and was attracted there by tales of its fine scotch and even more wonderful 
courtesans.


  Here is the financial report for Dances's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Dances was left with 6 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Naram
To: Dances

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I prepared my forces to defend the Pac. Ocean 1105 and the 
surrounding provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Naram


